        {
          "id": 731970313,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I wound up here because the [“Display Filter Expression” dialog box](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html/#ChWorkFilterAddExpressionSection) leave the statusbar in a bad state. \n```\nAnalyze->Display Filter Expression...\n```\nField Name - 29West  \nRelation - in  \nCancel  \n  \nThe statusbar now has the last dfilter test warning message.  \n  \nThere can also be more than one “Display Filter Expression” dialog box open concurrently, all updating the statusbar with messages while also updating their \"hint\" line with syntax messages. Another solution might be to move the statusbar updates out of display_filter_edit and let each calling function decide if the statusbar should be updated.\n  \nThe follow up (future MR) to this would be to find all the places a display filter can be entered and copy/reuse the code from the “Display Filter Expression” dialog box that updates the \"hint\" line.  \n  \nAnother example (IO graph dfilter) where the hint and statusbar duplicate information:  \n  \n![211112_iog_dfilter](/uploads/3ccf00a2e0fbb455cb85f66445eac0b3/211112_iog_dfilter.png)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-11-12T14:21:09.502Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-11-12T14:28:04.890Z",
